course: dictionary
lesson: 8317
title: Robocall: a word from phone and online safety
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A robocall is a phone call made by a computer, not a person. The computer plays a recorded message to many people at once. The word is a mix of robot and call, so the clue is in the name. «Automated phone calls, or robocalls, use recorded or AI voices.» Automated means done by a machine without a person doing each step.
explain: Read the words around robocall to find its meaning. «Some are surveys and some are scams.» A survey asks you questions, and a scam is a trick to take your money or your details. So a robocall can be useful or can be a trick, and the context tells you which.
explain: In one news report, «a robocall used an AI copy of President Biden's voice to tell people not to vote.» The people behind it were fined, which means they had to pay money as a punishment. This is a real example of why we must be careful with phone calls.
fact: A robocall is an automatic phone call with a recorded or computer-made voice.
fact: To robocall means to make calls like this to many people.
fact: Some robocalls are useful, such as a message that school is closed or an appointment reminder.
fact: Some robocalls are scams: if a recorded voice says you owe money or a parcel is waiting, hang up and do not press any number.
fact: The word robocall is common in the USA and Canada.
exercise: «Automated phone calls, or robocalls, use recorded or AI voices.» What does automated mean here? | Something that happens only once a year | Sent by post | *Done by a machine, without a person doing each step | Done by a person who is very slow
exercise: What is a robocall? | A letter delivered to your home by a postman | *A phone call made by a computer that plays a recorded message to many people | A phone call from your best friend | A robot who visits you at school
exercise: A recorded voice says your parcel is waiting and you must press 1 now. What should you do? | Give your bank details over the phone | *Hang up and tell an adult | Call the number back and ask lots of questions | Press 1 quickly
test: Some robocalls are useful. Which one is an example? | A recorded voice saying your account is locked | *A message telling you the school is closed today | A scam asking for your password | A call that tells you a prize is waiting
test: What does the verb to robocall mean? | *To make automatic calls with recorded messages to many people | To answer your phone with a person's voice | To hang up on a rude caller | To ring a bell at school
exam: The word robocall is a mix of two words. Which two? | robin and call | rob and cal | *robot and call | roll and call
